; A comment may follow the price of a price directive, as it may follow
; the amount of a posting, with or without white-space before its
; semicolon (#3353).  So may one follow a price written as an
; expression, which ends at its closing parenthesis: the semicolon used
; to continue the expression, which then failed to evaluate the comment.

P 2024/01/01 EUR $1.10 ; a comment after a space
P 2024/01/02 EUR $1.20; a comment right after the price
P 2024/01/03 EUR ($1.00 + $0.30)	; a comment after a tab
P GBP $1.50 ; a comment on a line without a date

apply fixed CAD $0.75 ; a comment after a fixed price
2024/01/04 Buy
    Assets:Cash                           10 CAD
    Equity
end apply fixed

test pricedb --now 2030/06/15
P 2024/01/01 00:00:00 EUR $1.10
P 2024/01/02 00:00:00 EUR $1.20
P 2024/01/03 00:00:00 EUR $1.30
P 2030/06/15 00:00:00 GBP $1.50
end test

test print
2024/01/04 Buy
    Assets:Cash                         10 CAD {=$0.75}
    Equity
end test
